# New provider onboarding

Invoke with `@new-provider-onboarding` when adding a new LLM, vision, or video-generation
provider.

1. Implement the provider-abstraction interface (`14-provider-abstraction-mcp.mdc`) — no
   bespoke call sites in pipeline nodes.
2. Register its capability class and where it sits in the fallback order for that class.
3. Configure circuit-break thresholds (default: 5 failures / 30s unless there's a reason
   to differ).
4. Add a cost + latency benchmark test (feeds the >20% cost regression CI gate).
5. If it's a model (not Higgsfield), add it at the LiteLLM gateway under the correct
   logical alias and update `02-model-routing.mdc`'s table.
6. Ship behind a feature flag; if it changes an existing prompt/model path, follow
   `docs/playbooks/prompt-change-rollout-playbook.md` (10% traffic first).
7. Update `docs/architecture/adr/0004-higgsfield-mcp-provider-abstraction.md` (or a new
   ADR) if this changes the fallback topology, not just adds a leaf.
